  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "FAIL",
      "title": "Global view permission bypasses client-specific denials",
      "description": "`canView(ClientModel)` returns immediately when `canView()` grants the all-clients `view` permission, without evaluating permissions for the requested client. Consequently, an explicit client-specific denial cannot override that global grant. `ClientsResource.getClients()` also uses the global result to return full representations without per-client checks.\n\nThis differs from the override behavior implemented in `UserPermissionsV2` and exercised by `UserResourceTypeEvaluationTest.testViewUserPermission`. Reserve the unconditional shortcut for administrative roles, and evaluate fine-grained view permissions against the specific client before falling back to the all-clients resource. Add tests combining a global grant with a client-specific denial for both direct reads and listing.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "security-hygiene",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/ClientPermissionsV2.java:78-82"
    },
    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "All-clients manage permission does not allow listing client scopes",
      "description": "The global `canView()` check recognizes only the `view` scope, although the new client-scope methods explicitly recognize `manage` as sufficient to view and manage client scopes.\n\nInherited `canViewClientScopes()` delegates to `canView()`, and `ClientScopesResource.getClientScopes()` uses that result to decide whether to return any scopes. An administrator granted only all-clients `manage` can therefore create client scopes but receives an empty scope listing when holding `query-clients`, or a forbidden response without that role. Include the global `manage` grant in the appropriate listing/view checks and cover a manage-only permission in the client-scope REST tests.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "correctness",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/ClientPermissionsV2.java:86-88"
    }
  ],
